{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Mass of Gold: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja56'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 56 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Āsīsavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Hope </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>6. Kañcanakkhandhajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Mass of Gold: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yo pahaṭṭhena cittena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>He whose heart is well-forged, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pahaṭṭhamanaso naro; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a man of cheerful mind, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bhāveti kusalaṁ dhammaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>develops skillful qualities </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yogakkhemassa pattiyā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for the sake of sanctuary from the yoke. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pāpuṇe anupubbena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Gradually he would attain </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sabbasaṁyojanakkhayan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the ending of all fetters. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Kañcanakkhandhajātakaṁ chaṭṭhaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
